// Arrays: `#variable A[3]` is three declarations, addressed by subscript.
//
// A constant subscript folds to the element's own declaration and costs no
// instruction. A RUNTIME subscript becomes an OP_SETOX in front of the access,
// which shifts the base by one element and is bounds checked against the length
// baked into it.
//
// Reads lag one cycle -- the transaction model, not the arrays -- so the
// expectations here are the settled values.

#variable A[3] = 0
#variable I = 0
#variable J = 0
#variable x = 0
#variable y = 0
#variable z = 0

// Constant subscripts, one per element.
A[0] = 10 ? 1
A[1] = 20 ? 1
A[2] = 30 ? 1

// A with no subscript is element 0 -- the head IS the first element, which is
// what makes a scalar and a one-element array the same thing.
z = A ? 1

// Runtime subscripts, reading two different elements through the same
// declaration. If OP_SETOX were not applied per access, or if the register
// cache in map_reg were allowed to serve an array, x and y would come out equal.
I = 1 ? 1
J = 2 ? 1
x = A[I] ? 1
y = A[J] ? 1
